      "anatomy_region": "胚胎及發育",
      "stem": "下列何者與胚胎性別分化（sex differentiation）最相關 ？",
      "options": {
        "A": "Müllerian-inhibiting substance（MIS）",
        "B": "follicle-stimulating hormone（FSH）",
        "C": "androgen-binding protein",
        "D": "inhibin"
      },
      "option_A": "Müllerian-inhibiting substance（MIS）",
      "option_B": "follicle-stimulating hormone（FSH）",
      "option_C": "androgen-binding protein",
      "option_D": "inhibin",
      "option_E": "",
      "option_count": 4,
      "answer": "A",
      "correct_answers": [
        "A"
      ],
      "answer_credit_type": "standard",
      "answer_note": "",
      "explanation": "胚胎男性性分化關鍵之一是睪丸 Sertoli cell 分泌 Müllerian-inhibiting substance（MIS，又稱 AMH），促使 Müllerian duct 退化，避免形成輸卵管、子宮與上段陰道。",
      "option_analysis": {
        "A": "正確。MIS 是胚胎性別分化的重要訊號，促使 Müllerian duct 退化。",
        "B": "錯。FSH 主要調控青春期後的性腺功能，不是胚胎性別分化的主要決定因子。",
        "C": "錯。androgen-binding protein 由 Sertoli cell 產生，幫助維持局部 androgen 濃度，但不是性分化最核心訊號。",
        "D": "錯。inhibin 主要抑制 FSH 分泌，與胚胎 Müllerian duct 退化不是最直接相關。"
      },
      "exam_point": "MIS/AMH 造成 Müllerian duct 退化；testosterone 維持 Wolffian duct；DHT 形成外生殖器男性化。",
      "difficulty": "中偏難",
